            "U",
            "According to the earliest surviving biography of the saint, known as <i>L'Assidua</i>, Bonovillo confronted Anthony directly. He declared that he would renounce his heresy only if a mule he had deliberately starved for three days, when set before both fodder and a consecrated host, would choose to adore the host rather than eat."
